``py-version`` now defaults to the lower bound of ``requires-python`` in the closest
``pyproject.toml``, instead of to the interpreter running pylint. Projects that support
an older Python than the one they develop on will see the version dependent checks fire
where they used to stay silent, for instance ``using-generic-type-syntax-in-unsupported-version``.
Set ``py-version`` explicitly to keep the old behaviour. Only ``>=`` and ``~=`` lower
bounds are read; anything else still falls back to the running interpreter.

Closes #11688
